exam: It is given that {a} possesses {n} {t} and relinquishes one {p.ordwords} thereof. Determine the number of {t} remaining in {a.his} possession.
exam: Ascertain the number of {t} remaining in a box which originally contained {n} {t}, one {p.ordwords} of them having been removed.
exam: Whereas one {p.ordwords} of a stock of {n} {t} has been consumed, state the quantity of {t} not so consumed.
exam: Compute the remainder when one {p.ordwords} of a set of {n} {t} is withdrawn from the set.
exercise: {a} keeps {n} goldfish. Over the winter one {p.ordwords} of them crossed the rainbow bridge. How many goldfish are still alive?
exercise: A factory has {n} workers, and one {p.ordwords} of them are made redundant. How many workers keep their jobs?
test: some joker took a "five-finger discount" on a {p.ordwords} of our {n} {t}. bloody thieves. how many we got left
